      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TIMMY TURTLE NZ (8) is racing well at this circuit and distance, scoring a second-up win in good style two back before fighting well to miss narrowly last week. Shouldn't spend a penny from this draw and sprint lane may come in handy. Race fit now and has strong claims. KENNYS SON (4) continued the strong form when he came from the back row and scored last start at Maryborough, his third success from his last four attempts. Has the benefit of a good draw and owns a strong record at this circuit and distance. Big chance to get the job done again. WAIKARE ADRIENNA (1) steps up in grade but has put two wins together and should get every chance from the inside draw. ALDEBARAN SUE (10) found winning form here last start. Cops a tricky draw but goes well at this shorter distance with a win and a placing from two attempts. CHARLESTON AVENUE (11) is another that might require luck from a tough draw but the form reads well.",
